      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Example: Tag Chain -> Recipe Map -> Batch Sampler -> Save Batch Folder.\n\n1. Tag Chain turns the base prompt plus one add/remove step per line into a 4-line recipe (4 images).\n2. Recipe Map appends the same text to every line (each / pairwise / by_index).\n3. Batch Sampler samples one image per recipe line and returns the resolved prompt for each image on its 'prompts' output.\n4. Save Batch Folder stores the batch and writes those prompts into the PNG metadata (fish_tags) - connect 'prompts' to its 'tags' input.\n\nStyle Permute below is muted: unmute it (right click -> Mode) to expand style tags into every combination or permutation instead of using Tag Chain.\nSwap the checkpoint for any SDXL/SD1.5 model you have."
      ],
      "title": "How this example works"
    }
